  "narrative": {
    "intro": "FY2027 to date federal contract obligations in Indiana total $54.5M. The Department of Veterans Affairs leads buying activity with $47.7M in obligations. Obligations fell 98.8% year over year, and the state recorded 905 awards with an average award size of $60.3K. Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations with $15.7M, followed by Special Needs Transportation at $6.5M and Electromedical and Electrotherapeutic Apparatus Manufacturing at $4.3M. ROCHE DIAGNOSTICS CORPORATION is the largest vendor with $19M in obligations, followed by AFTER ACTION MEDICAL AND DENTAL SUPPLY, LLC at $4.3M and INDIANA UNIVERSITY HEALTH CARE ASSOCIATES, INC. at $3.7M. FY22 through FY26 annual obligations were much larger than the current fiscal year to date, including $8.2B in FY22, $5.3B in FY24, $7B in FY25, and $4.6B in FY26. Current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date reporting.",
    "sections": [
