        "heading": "What changed in FY2027 to date compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 98.8% year over year. FY27 to date obligations total $54.5M, compared with prior full fiscal years such as $8.2B in FY22 and $4.6B in FY26. The award count is 905 and the average award size is $60.3K, reflecting smaller or fewer awards so far in the fiscal year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate Indiana federal spending?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer with $47.7M in obligations, followed by the Department of Justice with $5.5M and the General Services Administration with $736K. ROCHE DIAGNOSTICS CORPORATION is the top vendor at $19M, followed by AFTER ACTION MEDICAL AND DENTAL SUPPLY, LLC at $4.3M and INDIANA UNIVERSITY HEALTH CARE ASSOCIATES, INC. at $3.7M."
      }
    ]
